      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nReport when MRV1 skips draft generation because a batch exceeds the draft model's context limit. This makes an existing speculative-decoding fallback visible.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\nWhen one sequence exceeds the limit, the current code silently skips drafting for the entire batch, including shorter requests. Those requests lose speculative decoding for that step without a message that explains the cause.\r\n\r\nThe change emits one warning per context limit and identifies `speculative_config.max_model_len`. It preserves the existing fallback, scheduling, and generated tokens.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py \\\r\n  -k draft_context_limit_warning --noconftest -q\r\npre-commit run --files vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py \\\r\n  tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe two regression cases passed on macOS arm64 with Python 3.12.13. They cover the exact boundary, the first over-limit input, the extra DFlash query token, and missing attention metadata. The cases call the real runner method with minimal metadata. `--noconftest` excludes unrelated GPU fixtures.\r\n\r\nRestoring the predicate from main in memory makes both cases fail because no warning is emitted. All applicable pre-commit hooks passed. The test remains in the existing worker suite, and the Buildkite test-tethering hook passed.\r\n\r\nA GPU serving reproduction of the warning remains pending. No model evaluation or throughput improvement is claimed. The Testing and Validation item remains open until the serving reproduction is complete.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n`_input_fits_in_drafter()` compares the maximum sequence length plus draft query tokens against `effective_drafter_max_model_len`. A false result takes the existing fallback that suppresses draft tokens for the batch.\r\n\r\nThe warning uses the existing `warning_once` helper and a stable context-limit argument. It adds no GPU reads or synchronization. Increasing the draft limit is appropriate only when the draft model supports the requested length.\r\n\r\nThis is a diagnostic for deployments that still use MRV1. MRV2 uses separate speculator implementations and does not call this predicate, so this PR does not port the legacy warning into MRV2.\r\n\r\nOpen-PR searches for draft context-limit warnings found no other PR with this runtime diagnostic. #52546 concerns a configuration-time warning about an ignored setting.\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used to prepare and test this change.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\r\n",
